7. Download your installation pull secret from the Red Hat OpenShift Cluster Manager 
https://console.redhat.com/openshift/install/pull-secret

8. RHCOS doesn't follow the OCP z-stream numbering reliable approach is to ask your 4.18.22 openshift-install which boot image it expects
# Exact URLs this installer expects
openshift-install coreos print-stream-json > rhcos-stream.json

ISO_URL=$(jq -r '.architectures.x86_64.artifacts.metal.formats.iso.disk.location' rhcos-stream.json)
RAW_URL=$(jq -r '.architectures.x86_64.artifacts.metal.formats."raw.gz".disk.location' rhcos-stream.json)
echo $ISO_URL; echo $RAW_URL

Download ISO and Raw images
curl -L -O "$ISO_URL"
curl -L -O "$RAW_URL"

